  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilient Cities Nature-based Urban Resilience Through Unifying and Responsive Engagement (CRC-NURTURE) - CARA Flexible Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project strengthen the resilience in the climate-vulnerable Philippine cities of Legazpi, Borongan, and Zamboanga by integrating climate risk-informed Nature-based Solutions (NbS) into local planning and development systems. Building on prior CRC work, the project enhances institutional capacities through governance mechanisms, targeted training modules, and stakeholder engagement anchored on climate, socio-economic, and ecological data. It also supports the co-development and implementation of gender-responsive pilot NbS projects, alongside resource mobilization support. By embedding NbS into planning processes and demonstrating locally appropriate models, the project will enables cities to advance nature-positive, inclusive, and scalable urban resilience strategies.</narrative>
  </description>
